---
description: Pack and publish Svartz workspace packages without leaking workspace dependency specs
globs:
  - packages/*/package.json
  - themes/*/package.json
  - scripts/*release*.mjs
  - .github/workflows/*release*.yml
  - .github/workflows/package-publish.yml
alwaysApply: false
---

# Package release

- Pack public packages with pnpm. It converts `workspace:` dependencies to npm-compatible ranges. Publish the exact tarballs with npm. `npm pack` leaves workspace specs unresolved.
- Keep every public package at the same v1 version. Publish dependencies before `svartz`, because `npx svartz@latest init` installs the others from npm.
- Validate the packed archives in a temporary project outside the monorepo. Source imports and workspace symlinks hide missing package files and dependency declarations.
- The CLI's Vite dependency is a peer. A Vite 8 host must resolve its own Vite 8 through the packed CLI. `@svartz/vite` also peers on the host's Svelte Vite plugin: v6 for Vite 7, v7 for Vite 8. Exercise protected SVX in the packed Vite 8 host. Tailwind scans `dist` in packed theme/UI packages and their runtime dependency or component-library peer packages, never dev-only tooling.
- Type-check generated routes in the packed host with the `@svartz/vite/virtual-modules` reference. The older UI reference has a narrower runtime index and does not type-check host discovery helpers.
- All public packages use MCX v1.0. Keep the repository `LICENSE` in each package root and verify its packed text.
- Every public package declares `repository` with `url` `https://github.com/mia-cx/svartz.git` and its own `directory`; npm provenance requires the URL, and the packed manifest is checked.
- Before changing versioning or workflows, read `docs/releasing.md` for bootstrap, OIDC setup, and release authorization.
- Theme manifest package versions follow Changesets. Keep exactly one `version: 'x.y.z',` field in each theme's `src/lib/manifest.ts`, shared by its build and runtime extensions; `scripts/release-version.mjs` synchronizes that path. Keep their v1 contract versions separate.
- Release checks must accept later fixed-group versions and build the packed Vite 8 Cloudflare host, including Worker and mounted note output.
